## Critical: Syntax Validator Compatibility

QUpload validates all uploaded PHP files using `token_get_all($content, TOKEN_PARSE)` before activation. This is the source plugin that enforces the compatibility constraint.

### BLOCKED Patterns (Never Use)

| Pattern | Replacement |
|---------|-------------|
| `is_array($var)` | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpArray->value` |
| `is_string($var)` | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpString->value` |
| `is_int($var)` | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpInteger->value` |
| `is_float($var)` | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpDouble->value` |
| `is_bool($var)` | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpBoolean->value` |
| `is_object($var)` | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpObject->value` |
| `is_null($var)` | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpNull->value` |
| `array()` constructor | Use `[]` short syntax |
| Magic type strings | Use `PhpNativeType` enum values |

### SAFE Patterns

`in_array()`, `array_merge()`, `array_filter()`, `array_map()`, `array_key_exists()` — all safe (tokenize as T_STRING).

### PhpNativeType Enum

Located at `includes/Enums/PhpNativeType.php`:

```php
use QUpload\Enums\PhpNativeType;

gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpArray->value
```

