## PHP Coding Rules

- Catch `Throwable`, never `Exception`
- Always log stack traces
- Use `ErrorLogHelper::log($e, 'Context:')` or `::logAndThrow($e, ...)`
- Positive boolean names only (`$isValid`, `$hasData`)
- Extract ternary conditions to named booleans
- Maximum 15 lines per function, 300 lines per file
- ABSPATH guard after namespace (never before)
- Namespaced files: `PascalCase.php`

